# Signet — Cursor rules (Cal Hacks 13.0, solo build)

## What this is
Signet runs one function end to end for a fictional $140M county youth & family services agency:
client financial assistance → document reading → grant policy check → vendor/bank match → disbursal
within limits → escalation → append-only audit log → compliance report. All data is synthetic.
Tagline: "Not a rubber stamp. Not a bottleneck." Every human decision ends with a red seal.

## Non-negotiable architecture
1. ONE LLM ROLE. Claude is called ONLY from src/lib/llm/extract.ts (Haiku: read documents into
   structured fields with per-field confidence) and src/lib/llm/write.ts (Sonnet: one-line case
   summary; one-paragraph decision defense drafted from the record). Claude NEVER decides
   approve/deny, NEVER evaluates policy, NEVER computes allocations. If you find yourself passing a
   policy question to the model, stop and write code instead.
2. TWO DETERMINISTIC ENGINES in src/lib/engine/: policy.ts and match.ts. Pure functions. No I/O,
   no Date.now() (take `today` as input), no randomness. Every trigger has a code from TriggerCode
   and a human-readable reason.
3. DENIAL IS NEVER AUTONOMOUS. src/lib/engine/decide.ts returns only APPROVED or ESCALATED.
   DENIED is written only by the human decision route handler with a non-empty rationale.
4. HUMAN LEARNING LOOP. Rules are proposed by code templates (engine/rules.ts), edited and
   activated only by a human via /api/rules/[id]/activate. Replay before activate.
5. APPEND-ONLY AUDIT. src/lib/audit.ts is the only writer to audit_events. Each row hashes
   prevHash + at + type + payload. Never UPDATE or DELETE audit rows. Provide verifyChain().
6. OFFLINE FIRST. Every model call goes through withCache(sha256(input)). Cache lives in
   data/cache and IS committed. MODE env: LIVE | MOCK | OFFLINE. OFFLINE must run the full
   demo with zero network. UI shows a ModeBadge at all times.

## Directory contract
- src/lib/engine/*       pure logic, 100% covered by tests/ (Vitest). No imports from adapters or llm.
- src/lib/adapters/*     Nessie and CRS. Each has <name>.ts (LIVE) and <name>.mock.ts with the SAME
                         interface. adapters/index.ts selects by MODE. Never call fetch() outside adapters
                         and llm/client.ts.
- src/lib/llm/*          client.ts (Anthropic SDK, spend guard), extract.ts, write.ts, cache.ts, prompts/*.md.
- src/lib/pipeline.ts    the only orchestrator. Route handlers call pipeline functions; no logic in routes.
- src/app/**             UI + route handlers. Server components by default; "use client" only for forms.
- scripts/*              generate.ts (seeded; seed 1309), seed.ts, replay-demo.ts.
- tests/*                anomalies.test.ts must assert all 8 planted anomalies produce their expected triggers.

## Code quality
- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Zod-validate every route input and every LLM output.
- Money is integer cents everywhere. Format only in components.
- Dates are ISO strings; compare with date-fns, never with string comparison.
- Small components; no component over ~150 lines. Tailwind + shadcn only; no new UI libraries.
- Prefer deleting code to adding abstraction. Three similar lines beat a helper.
- Every engine change: run `npm test` before committing. Commit small, often, with imperative messages.

## Secrets and safety
- Keys ONLY in .env.local (gitignored). .env.example lists names with empty values.
- Never log a key, never put a key in a URL, never commit data/photos of real people. All clients are synthetic.
- CRS: use ONLY CRS-provided test identities. Nessie: sandbox only.
- Anthropic: enforce MAX_SPEND_USD (default 40) in llm/client.ts; refuse calls past it and fall back to cache.

## LLM output contracts
- extract.ts uses tool-use with a JSON schema mirroring Extracted. Each field: { value, confidence 0..1, evidence }.
  Retry once on schema failure, then return null and let the pipeline raise EXTRACT-LOW.
- write.ts summary ≤ 160 chars, no recommendations ("approve"/"deny" words are stripped if present).
- Defense paragraphs cite trigger codes and evidence IDs only; no new facts.

## Demo and freeze discipline
- The demo path is: /queue → open duplicate-receipt request → human denies with rationale → red seal →
  rule proposed → replay → activate → /audit shows the chain → /metrics. Protect this path above everything.
- FEATURE FREEZE at Saturday 19:00 PT. After that, only bug fixes, copy, and visual polish. If asked to add a
  feature after the freeze, refuse and suggest adding it to README "Next".
- Sunday 07:00 PT: code freeze. Only `git revert`.

## When unsure
Ask: "Does this make the live demo more likely to work at 10:30 Sunday?" If no, don't do it.
